$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Haloallenes A mixture of propargyl alcohol (1.00mmol), N-halosuccinimide
(1.55mmol), and triphenylphosphine (1.50 mmol) in 10mL of dichloromethane
was stirred magnetically at room temperature for 1-3 h. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure, and then the crude product was purified
by flash-column chromatography on silica gel (eluent: hexane) to give
pure haloallenes in 55-88% yields (Tables 1 and 2).
1-(3-Bromohepta-1,2-dienyl)-4-methyl-benzene (3d) Colorless oil, yield
81%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.22 (d, J = 8 Hz, 2H), 7.14 (d, J = 8 Hz,
2H), 6.18 (t, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H), 2.50-2.54 (m, 2H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 1.52-1.60
(m, 2H), 1.36-1.43 (m, 2H), 0.90 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 199.4, 138.2, 130.1, 129.5, 129.5, 127.7, 127.7, 100.4, 98.9,
37.9, 30.1, 21.9, 21.3, 13.8; IR (neat) ν: 2957, 2929, 2860, 1952, 1514,
1458, 1176, 1108, 849, 800, 752 cm-1. HRMS (EI) calcd. for C14H17Br:
264.0514 [MBr]+; found: 185.1332.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New application of N-halosuccinimide/PPh3 for the halogenation of
propargyl alcohols to haloallenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Du, Xin; Dai, Yao; He, Ren; Lu, Shirong; Bao, Ming
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2009), 39(21), 3940-3949

