$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1,4-Bis[dialkyl(2,3,4,5-tetrabromo-2-pentenyl)-ammonio]-2-butene
dibromides IIIa-IIId. A tenfold molar excess of bromine was added
dropwise with continuous stirring at room temperature to an aqueous
solution of 0.03 mol of Ia-Id. After 4 h the resulting complex was washed
with five 50-ml portions of water and dried. Decomposition of the
complexes with acetone (chemically pure grade) yielded compounds
IIIa-IIId, which were recrystallized from diethyl ether. Compound IIId.
Yield: 80%. R f: 0.78; IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 590, 1600, 1615; UV
spectrum, λmax,nm: 232; Formula: C30H52Br10N2; ; 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm
(J, Hz)a: 0.99 t [12H, N(CH2)3CH3, J 8.0], 1.42 m (8H, CH2CH2CH3), 1.84 m
(8H, CH2CH2C2H5), 3.53 m (8H, CH2C3H7), 3.92 m and 3.96 m (4H, CH2Br),
4.42 br.d (4H, CH2CH=, J -5.5), 4.72 and 4.90 d.d (4H, CH2CBr=, Jgem
15.0), 5.80 d.d (2H, CHBr, J 1 10.8, J 2 5.7), 6.68 br.t (2H, CH=CH, J
-5.5)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of
1,4-bis[dialkyl(2,3,4,5-tetrabromo-2-pentenyl)ammonio]-2-butene
dibromides
