$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,2-trans-Dibromocyclohexane, 6. C60Br8 (100 mg, 0.074 mmol) was
dissolved in 30 mL of 1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane followed by the addition
of 1 mL of cyclohexene (excess). The reaction mixture was refluxed for 12
hours. Subsequently the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature
and all volatiles removed. The residue was chromatographed on a silica
column using hexane as the eluent, 14 mg, 78%.
