$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM trans-1,2-Dibromocyclohexane (9) from a reaction in dichloromethane. A
stirring bar, 0.17 mL (2.0 mmol) of cyclohexene and 2.0 mL of
dichloromethane were placed into a 4 mL brown vial. A PTFE sealed tube
filled with 0.11 mL (2.2 mmol) of bromine was inserted into the solution.
It took about 5 minutes for bromine to diffuse into the solution.
Evaporation of dichloromethane gave 0.45 g (93%) of crude
trans-1,2-dibromocyclohexane (9). Bulb-to-bulb distillation under a
reduced pressure gave 0.34 g (70%) of pure trans-1,2-dibromocyclohexane
(9). trans-1,2-Dibromocyclohexane (9), yield 0.34 g (70%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, phase-vanishing reaction, PFTE tape (teflon tape) used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phase-Vanishing Reactions with PTFE (Teflon) as a Phase Screen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Van Zee, Nathan J.; Dragojlovic, Veljko
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2009), 11(15), 3190-3193

