$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of quinone imines Ia-Ic-IIIa-IIIc,
XXXIIIa , XXXIIIb,XXXIVa, XXXIVb , and aminophenols XIIa-XIIc-XIVa-XIVc ,
XLIVa,XLIVb, XLIXa, and XLIXb. To a solution of 2 mmol of compounds under
study in 3 ml of CHCl3, AcOH, DMF or a mixture DMF-AcOH, 1:5, was added
dropwise at stirrng a bromine solution in an appropriate solvent to the
desired ratio initial compound-bromine (1:1, 1:3, 1:5, 1:8). The reaction
products obtained in several hours were filtered off, washed with acetic
acid, and recrystallized from acetic acid.
5,6-Dibromo-3,5-dimethyl-4-tosylimino-2-cyclohexen-1-one (XXXVIb). Yield
79%. mp 140-141°C.1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 6.34 q (1H, H 2 ), 4.73 d (1H,
H 6 ), 2.57 d (3H, Me 3 ),2.00 s [3H, Me 5 , J(H 2 , Me 3 )1.2, J(H 2 ,
6)1.5 Hz], 7.36-7.86 d.d (4H in Ts), 2.46 s (3H, Me in Ts). Found, %: Br
35.68, 35.76. C35H15Br2NO3S. Calculated, %: Br 35.58.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no experimental detail
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of N-substituted para-quinone monoimine and para-quinone
monooxime esters: V. Chlorination and bromination of
N-arylsulfonyl-1,4-benzoquinone monoimines dialkyl-substituted in the
quinoid ring
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Avdeenko, A. P.; Konovalova, S. A.
