$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl 2,3,3-tribromo-3-nitropropanoate (2a).
Bromine (3.86 g, 1.2 mL, 0.024 mol) was added to a solution of methyl
3-bromo-3-nitroacrylate (1a) (2.54 g, 0.012 mol) in CCl4 (25 mL) and the
reaction mixture was refluxed on a sand bath for 24 h. After evaporation
of the solvent and excess of bromine on the Petri dish, the residue (4 g)
was purified by column chromato-graphy. From the fraction eluted with
CCl4. Ethyl 2,3,3-tribromo-3-nitropropanoate (2b) was synthesized
similarly to compound 2a from ethyl 3-bromo-3-nitroacrylate (1b) (3 g,
0.0138 mol) and bromine (4.4 g, 1.4 mL, 0.0276 mol) in CCl4 (30 mL)
(refluxing for 20 h). The crude product (4.51 g) was purified by
chromatography. From the fraction eluted with CCl4. Compound 2b (4.2 g,
79%) was obtained. Found (%): C, 15.84; H, 1.41. C5H6Br3NO4. Calculated
(%): C, 15.65; H, 1.58. R f 0.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and structure of alkyl 2,3-dibromo-3-nitroacrylates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Makarenko, S. V.; Kovalenko, K. S.; Krivolapov, D. B.; Litvinov, I. A.;
Berestovitskaya, V. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Chemical Bulletin (2009), 58(10), 2039-2042

