$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of quinone imines
Ia-Ic-IIIa-IIIc, XXXIIIa , XXXIIIb , XXXIVa, XXXIVb , and aminophenol s
XIIa-XIIc-XIVa-XIVc , XLIVa, XLIVb, XLIXa, and XLIXb. Through a solution
of 2 mmol of compounds under study in 3 ml of CHCl3, AcOH, DMF or a
mixture DMF-AcOH, 1:5, was passed a steam of dry chlorine at a rate 15-20
ml/min at 25 -30°C. The ratio initial substance-chlorine was controlled
by the weight gain, and it was varied in the range 1 : 1 -1:3. In several
hours the reaction products were filtered off. All compounds obtained
were recrystallized from acetic acid.
2-Isopropyl-5-methyl-4-phenylsulfonylimino-5,6-
dichloro-2-cyclohexen-1-one (VIIa). Yield 78%. mp 98-100°C.1H NMR
spectrum, δ, ppm: 7.82 d (1H, H 3 ), 4.52 s (1H, H 6 ),3.07 m [1H, (CH) 2
], 1.86 s (3H, Me 5 ), 1.16-1.25 d.d {6H, Me 2 in i-Pr, J[(CH) 2 , H 3
]1.2 Hz}, 7.56-8.02 m (5H, Ph). Found, %: Cl 18.80, 18.85. C16H17Cl2NO3S.
Calculated, %: Cl 18.94.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no experimental detail
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of N-substituted para-quinone monoimine and para-quinone
monooxime esters: V. Chlorination and bromination of
N-arylsulfonyl-1,4-benzoquinone monoimines dialkyl-substituted in the
quinoid ring
