$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Benzophenone O-(1,2-dibromoethyl)oxime (II). A solution of 0.1 g (0.6
mmol) of bromine in 1 ml of dry methylene chloride was added with
stirring at room temperature to a solution of 0.13 g (0.6 mmol) of oxime
I in 1 ml of dry methylene chloride. The solution turned colorless. After
5 min, the solvent was removed under reduced pressure at 40°C. (purity
78%, according to the 1H NMR data). Light yellow transparent viscous
liquid, yield Yield 0.23 g (78%). nD20 = 1.6195. IR spectrum (film),
cm-1: 3085 w, 3058 m, 2983 m, 2924 w, 2852 w, 1657 m, 1597 m, 1578 w,
1492 m, 1445 s, 1420 m, 1367 w, 1341 m, 1327 m, 1306 m, 1278 m, 1220 m,
1205 w, 1169 m, 1146 m, 1110 s, 1075 m, 1038 w, 1026 m, 986 w, 965 s, 914
s, 871, 850 w, 830 w, 775 s, 696 s, 670 m, 650 m, 606 m, 585 s. 1H NMR
spectrum (CDCl3), δ , ppm: 7.52 d (2H, anti-o-H, 3Jo,m = 7.3 Hz), 7.32-
