$DATUM 1,2-trans-dichlorocyclohexane, 6. C60Cl6 (100 mg, 0.107 mmol) was
dissolved in 30mL of 1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane, followed by the addition
of 1 mL of cyclohexene to the reaction mixture. The reaction mixture was
refluxed for 12 hours. The solution was cooled to room temperature and
all volatiles removed. The residue was chromatographed on a silica column
using hexane as the eluent, Yield 12.5 mg, 76%.
