$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Allene Derivatives 2: CBr4 (331
mg, 1.0 mmol), Ph3P (262 mg, 1.0 mmol), propargylic alcohol 1 (0.50
mmol), i-Pr2NEt (129 mg, 1.0 mmol), P(n-Bu)3 (10 mg, 0.05 mmol), and a
freshly distilled toluene (1 mL) were successively added into a
screw-capped vial, and the vial was sealed with a cap containing a PTFE
septum. The reaction mixture was stirred at 100 °C, and monitored by TLC
until the propargylic alcohol 1 was consumed. To quench the reaction, H2O
(2 mL) was added to the mixture. The mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3
×), and the combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, filtered,
and then evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was
purified by silica gel chromatography(hexane) to produce the allene
derivative 2, and if necessary, was further purified by a recycling
preparative HPLC equipped with a GPC column (chloroform as an eluent).
1-(3-Bromo-1,2-nonadien-1-yl)benzene (2a), pale yellow oil, yield 76%. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.86 (t, 3 H, J = 7.2 Hz), 1.24-1.38 (m, 6 H),
1.50 (quint, 2 H, J = 7.2 Hz), 2.52 (td, 2 H, J = 7.2, 3.0 Hz), 6.19 (t,
1 H, J = 3.0 Hz), 7.23-7.27 (m, 1 H), 7.32-7.33 (m, 4 H). 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 13.9, 22.5, 27.9, 28.2, 31.4, 38.0, 96.1, 100.3, 127.7,
128.1, 128.7, 133.0, 199.8. MS (FAB): m/z (%) = 281 (100) [M+], 279 (40)
[M+]. HRMS (FAB): m/z calcd for C15H2OBr: 279.0748; found: 279.0726.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective, Appel type reaction, optimization study
(temperature, time, bases)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemoselective isomerization of secondary-type propargylic alcohols to
propargylic/allenic bromides, and brominated dienes with Appel-type
reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sakai, Norio; Maruyama, Tsukasa; Konakahara, Takeo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2009), (13), 2105-2108

