$DATUM Methyl 2,3,3-tribromo-3-nitropropanoate (2a). Bromine (3.86 g, 1.2 mL,
0.024 mol) was added to a solution of methyl 3-bromo-3-nitroacrylate (1a)
(2.54 g, 0.012 mol) in CCl4 (25 mL) and the reaction mixture was refluxed
on a sand bath for 24 h. After evaporation of the solvent and excess of
bromine on the Petri dish, the residue (4 g) was purified by column
chromato-graphy. From the fraction eluted with CCl4. Compound 2a (3.5 g,
76%) was obtained. Found (%): C, 13.41; H, 1.41; N, 4.26. C4H4Br3NO4.
Calculated (%): C, 12.99; H, 1.09; N, 3.79. R f 0.69.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
