$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 4,5-dibromopentanoate (17). A stirring bar, 0.200 g (2.0 mmol) of
4-pentenoic acid and 5.0 mL of ethanol were placed into a two-neck 25 mL
RB flask. The solution was heated to reflux and a PTFE (2 layers) sealed
tube filled with 0.12 mL (2.4 mmol) of bromine was inserted into the
flask. Bromine was consumed rapidly and the reaction was allowed to
proceed for a total of 15 min. Ethanol was evaporated under a reduced
pressure and the residue was chromatographed (Harrison Chromatotron,
eluting with 4:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate) to give 0.432 g (75%) of ethyl
4,5-dibromopentanoate (17). Ethyl 4,5-dibromopentanoate (17), yield 0.432
g (75%) 1H NMR (400 MHZ, CDCl3) δ: 1.25 (t, 3H, J = 7.1 Hz), 2.01 (m,
2H), 2.55 (m, 3H), 3.62 (dd, 1H, J = 10.4, 9.8), 3.85 (dd, 1H, J = 10.4,
4.5), 4.12 (q, 2H, J = 7.1), 4.23 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
14.2; 31.4; 31.7; 35.9; 51.6; 60.7; 172.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phase-vanishing reaction conditions, PFTE tape (teflon tape) used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phase-Vanishing Reactions with PTFE (Teflon) as a Phase Screen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Van Zee, Nathan J.; Dragojlovic, Veljko
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2009), 11(15), 3190-3193

