$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2,3-Dibromobut-2-ene-1,4-diylbis(dialkylamines) IIa-IIc. Aqueous HBr
(40%, 21 ml) was added drop-wise to 0.05 mol of
but-2-yne-1,4-diylbis(alkylamine). The resulting salt was treated in situ
at room temperature and vigorous stirring with 16 g of bromine, and the
complex of bromine with the corresponding amine hydrobromide was filtered
off. The UV spectra of all the complexes contain absorption bands at 220
and 270 nm (in the parent compounds, at 205 nm), characteristic for such
complexes. The complexes were decomposed with acetone (chemical grade).
Compound: Ia, Yield: 75%. Mp: 231°C, Rf: 0.46, 1HNMR spectra, δ, ppm (J,
Hz): 1.25 t (12H, CH2CH3, J7.5), 3.15-3.40 m (8H, CH2-CH3), 4.56 s (4H,
═CBrCH2), 9.60 br (2H, HBr). Formula: C12H26Br4N2, Found, %:Br: 31.06, N:
5.43, Calculated, %: Br: 30.88, N: 5.40, M: found: 516, calculated: 518.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and certain transformations of
2,3-dibromobut-2-ene-1,4-diylbis(dialkylamines)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Saakyan, T. A.; Gyul'nazaryan, A. Kh.; Markaryan, N. O.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2007), 77(9), 1519-1521

