$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of com pounds Ia-Ie, IVa-IVe, VIIIa, VIIIc-VIIIe. To 0.5 M
solution of a compound in an appropriate solvent was added dropwise at
vigorous stirring a solution of bromine in the same solvent with
concentration 3 mol-1. The reaction product was filtered off, washed with
a little acetic acid and methanol and crystallized from 2-propanol. The
bromination conditions, bromination products and certain features of the
products isolation are given in Table 2, characteristics of individual
compounds IIIa-IIId, Va-Vd, Xa, Xc and Xd are listed in Table 3. Number
of parent compound VIa: Yield 73% mp 145°C; C15H13Br2NO2
