$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-layer system for bromination reactions.
Normally, 1.2 equivalents of bromine (based on the substrate amount) were
added to a tube (10.5 mm diameter and 87 mm2 surface area) containing
perfluorohexane (~1.5 g; ~11 mm layer thickness). 1P10Br3 (~320 mg; ~5 mm
layer thickness) was added carefully to the top, followed by addition of
a solution of the substrate in hexadecane (2-2.5 mL). The tube was sealed
with a rubber stopper and kept in the dark during the period of reaction.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-reagent, in the dark, stereoselective, sealed tube used,
anti:syn=79:21, reagent prepared and used, stacked layers reactor used,
ionic liquid used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective Bromination Reactions Using Tridecylmethylphosphonium
Tribromide in a "Stacked" Reactor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ma, Kefeng; Li, Shaw; Weiss, Richard G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(19), 4155-4158

