$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The Preparation of
2-Chloro-3-(1,2-dibromo-3-quinolyl)-acrylic Ethyl Ester (7a-i): General
Procedure Bromine (0.18 mL, 0.0036 mole) in 10 mL of anhydrous chloroform
was added in a dropwise manner to a cooled, stirred suspension of
3-(2-chloro-3-quinolyl)acrylic ethyl ester (6a) (0.9 g, 0.0033 mole) in
20 mL of anhydrous chloroform, for about 30 min. Stirring and cooling was
continued for another 3 h. A light brown yellow powder resulted from
distilling out the solvent together with excess bromine. It was then
recrystallized from pet. ether:benzene (4:1 v/v) to yield creamy white
needles. Compound 7f, yield 71%. M.P.(°C): 140-141; IR (cm-1): 1730,
1069.
