$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Bromofluorination of
Alkenes with NBS/Dialkyl Ether/Poly(hydrogen fluoride) Complexes:
Preparation of 2-Bromo-3-fluoro-2,3-dimethyl-butane with NBS/DMEHF Two
grams of 2,3-dimethyl-2-butene was dissolved in 5 mL of CH2Cl2 in a 30-mL
polyethylene bottle. A premixed CH2Cl2 (10 mL) solution of 3 g of
N-bromosuccinimide (NBS) and DMEHF(1/5)was then added dropwise at -20 to
-30 °C. The reaction mixture was then stirred at room temperature for 2
h. The quenching and workup were carried out as described above. The
resulting organic solution was subjected to column chromatography (silica
gel, eluent: hexane). After solvent evaporation,
1-bromo-2-fluorocyclohexane 13C NMR : 22.6, (d, 3JC,F=7), 24.7, 31.0 (d,
2JC,F=21), 34.8 (d, 3JC,F=4), 52.6, (d, 2JC,F=21), 93.6, ( d, 2JC,F=181);
19F NMR : - 169 (m)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (HF is a volatile liq. with corrosive vapor - reaction of ether-HF
complexes with highly reactive substrates may cause exothermic reaction
and rapid gas evolution)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stable Dialkyl Ether/Poly(Hydrogen Fluoride) Complexes: Dimethyl
Ether/Poly(Hydrogen Fluoride), A New, Convenient, and Effective
Fluorinating Agent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bucsi, Imre; Toeroek, Bela; Marco, Alfonso Iza; Rasul, Golam; Prakash, G.
K. Surya; Olah, George A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2002), 124(26), 7728-7736

