$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Additions of Bromine and Bu4NBr3. (a) In
1,2-Dichloroethane. 1,2-Dichloroethane solutions of Br2 or Bu4NBr3 (5 mL,
10-2 M) were mixed with 5 mL of a 10-2 M solution of 2, or 3, or 4 or 5
in the same solvent. After the rapid disappearance of color the mixture
was evaporated (washed with water for the Bu4NBr3 reactions) and the
residue was analyzed by 1H and 13C NMR.
(2R,3S,6S)-6-Benzyloxymethyl-2,3-dibromo-tetrahydro-pyran, yield 95%; and
(2R,3R,6S)-6-Benzyloxymethyl-2,3-dibromo-tetrahydro-pyran, yield 5%.
