$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,6-Dibromo-4-(dichloromethyI)-4-methylcyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-one (6)
Bromine (0.627 g. 3.93 mmol) was added to the solution of dienone 1
(0.300 g. 1.57 mmol) in 10 ml of CCl4. The resulting mixture was stirred
for 1 day. NMR analysis of mixture showed the presence of two ketones 5
and 6 in a ratio of 1:14. Solvent and gaseous by-products were distilled
off in vacuo. The yellow residue was dissolved in diethyl ether
concentrated in vacuo, and redissolved in ether. After treatment with
alkaline Al2O3 ether was evaporated. The residue was purified by
silica-gel chromatography with benzene/diethyl ether mixture (5:0.3) as
eluent, Rf 0.84. The yield of dibromoketone 6 was 0.490 g (91 %). The
solid was dissolved in chloroform and precipitated by hexane.
2,6-Dibromo-4-(dichloromethyI)-4-methylcyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-one (6),
yield 0.490 g (91 %) Mp 109-112°C (lit. 120- 121°C[18], 172-174°C[19]).
UV, λmax, nm (lg ε) : 259 (4.30); IR: 1670 cm-1; 1H NMR: 7.43 (s, 2H, m.
H5). 5.77 (s, 1H, CHCl2), 1.58 (s, 3H. CH3); 13C NMR: 171.9 (CO), 148.9
(C3, C5). 124.2 (C2, C6). 75.1 (CHCl2). 53.8 (C4), 22.3 (CH3). Anal.
calcd. for C8H6Br2Cl2O: C. 27.50; H. 1.71. Found: C. 27.50: H, 1.65.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of 4-Dichloromethyl-4-methylcyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-ones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gavrilova, G. V.; Rusetskaya, I. N.; Gavrilov, A. A.; Trushkov, I. V.;
Krut'ko, D. P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
