$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: To a stirred mixture of
olefin (10 mmol) and KBr (35 mmol), CH3CN (25 mL), methanol or water (1
mL) and Selectfluor (13 mmol) was added. The reaction was monitored by
TLC. After completion of the reaction, it was diluted with water and
extracted with CH2Cl2 (25 mL x 3). The organic layers were combined and
washed with dilute solutions of NaHCO3, Na2SO3 and brine. It was dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure to give
crude products, which were purified by column chromatography packed with
silica gel to afford the pure products.
1-(1-bromo-2-methoxypropan-2-yl)benzene (3a) 1
(±)-trans-2-bromo-1,2-diphenylethanol (3f) 2 yield:89%
meso-1,2-dibromo-1,2-diphenylethane (4f) 3 yield:8%. (3f) 2:1H NMR δ 5.13
(d, 1H, J = 6.6 Hz), 5.21 (d, 1H, J = 6.6 Hz), 7.22-7.42 (m, 10H), 13C
NMR δ 59.9, 78.9, 128.0, 129.2, 129.3, 129.4, 129.7, 129.9, 138.6, 140.7.
(4f) 3:1H NMR δ 5.50 (s, 2H), 7.28-7.47 (m, 6H), 7.53-7.56 (m, 4H), 13C
NMR (CD3CN) δ 55.1, 126.9, 127.8, 128.0, 139.1.
